{
 "comment": "WP-AD.4 A-Diakoptics disposition overlay: one disposition per solvable_now.json entry point (bijective; corpus_ad_matches_normal_mode enforces it rust-vs-rust). ad = full|pf|off:<specific-reason>. Every disposition is evidence-backed by the empirical AD-init + AD-vs-normal snapshot-gap probe (DSS_AD_CLASSIFY=1); every ad-* deck was split into the D7 two legs (DSS_AD_DECOMPOSE: leg1=save round-trip orig-normal vs inter-normal, leg2=AD proper inter-normal vs AD) to attribute the gap. off reason classes: non-3ph-cut-only (D5 ZLL: only cut candidates are non-3-phase lines/transformers); too-small (Tear_Circuit cannot form two connected >=2-bus zones); already-torn-artifact (a pre-torn Torn_Circuit/zone master); mode-outside-AD-scope (dynamics/harmonics/faultstudy/monte/LD - AD is a snapshot/direct/time-series power-flow accelerator); save-roundtrip-{geometry,relpath,userdll,regxfmr,autotrans,relay} (the AD save+reload of Master_Interconnected.dss loses fidelity - the D7 ROUND-TRIP leg1, a save-circuit gap NOT an AD gap: the decomposition proves the AD leg proper (leg2) is CLEAN while leg1 carries the whole gap, e.g. the distance-relay decks leg1=2.4e3 / leg2=2.3e-15, IEEE13 leg1=5.9e-2 / leg2=1.6e-6; the autotrans decks have leg1>>1 so the save is the dominant proven defect and leg2 is measured against a corrupt baseline). The remaining ad-* classes are OPEN AD-engine defects (leg1 small, leg2 large = a genuine AD-vs-normal physics gap per section 5, filed in STATUS, kept off the gate because fixing the AD engine is outside WP-AD.4's sweep charter): ad-regulator-divergence (in-line/overexcitation regulator - ODRegTest leg2=1.5e15, TestDDRegulator leg2=0.88); ad-switched-divergence (open-switch/reconfiguration or meshed secondary - IEEE123Switches leg2=1.9e1, civanlar/SecPar leg2=1.0); ad-islanded-divergence (grid-forming/ISource microgrid with no firm source reference - GFM_IEEE123 leg2~7e5, Microgrid/ISource leg2=2.0); ad-nonconvergent (the AD snapshot did not even init/converge - the islanded GFM/GFL decks); ad-floor-above-tier (genuine long-radial stitch floor just above AD_SWEEP_TIER, IEEE34Mod1 leg2=2.1e-3 - NOT tolerance-widened per section 5). oracle names an EPRI rev for the D9(d) named cases.",
